ror)`; rev4 R05 replayed as R03 → KILLED ×2 by `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal` (`err top-level type = *axerror.Error … want *tmuxserver.Error`); the containment member (R02) KILLED ×2 by `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf`; the old-oracle replay proves the helper is load-bearing; `N-absence-remap-widen` shipped and KILLED ×2 in the producer harness; `N-background-absence-remap` kept. The ownership member of the same class is the residue (P3-A below) |\n59|| P2-B `Request.Name` re-opens the §3.2 path per call | **yes** | The field is gone (`grep -n Name acquire.go` finds only `RuntimeDirName`); `Acquire` passes `RuntimeDirName` at all three sites; `TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath` asserts the literal `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both callers; reviewer rows R04/R05/R06 (a `\"ax-tmux\"` literal at the lexical, ensure and verify sites respectively) KILLED ×2 by 18/8/6 tests including that test on the relevant caller |\n60|| P3-A absence remap pinned on macOS only | **yes** | `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` runs macos/linux/wsl2; rev4 R14 replayed as R07 → KILLED ×2 by the linux and wsl2 subtests exactly |\n61|| P3-B \"every background test arms a spy\" false for 4 of 11 | **yes** | Mechanical census: 12 background-path `Acquire` tests, 12 arm `spawnSpy` and assert zero calls (the 13th `CallerBackground` match is the helper test `TestCheckCreationAllowedRefusesBackground`, not an `Acquire` test); effect census R08 (a guarded direct-spawn plant at the top of `acquireBackground`) reddens 11 top-level tests / 20 lines — the 12th, `TestAcquireRefusesWindowsPlatform`, refuses at the lexical gate before the function is entered, which is correct. README and acquire.go:137 now scope the sentence to background-path `Acquire` tests and it is true |\n62|| Obs-1..5 | **yes** | row 6 ELOOP darwin-equivalence; B15 gains the unopenable-root, `Fchmod`, `Fsync` and leaf-`Stat` arms; B16 nested invocation (owner 1c28dz); row 23 live-member scoping; B19 caller-contract sentence |\n63|\n64|## P2 — must fix or record as a reviewed decision\n65|\n66|### P2-A. The background broker-or-refuse rule is pinned at the entry only for the fixture shapes: three realistic server-admission shapes and one realistic fallback guard walk through the committed suite\n67|\n68|SPEC §4.2 1419-1424: a background caller \"MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua\n69|broker and its **attested** AX tmux server; if neither exists it MUST return\n70|`capability_unavailable` … and MUST NOT fall back to direct server creation.\" The candidate\n71|implements both halves correctly (`CheckBrokerContact` → `CheckServerAttested`; no spawn call on\n72|the path; `checkCreationAllowed` consulted by call), and the committed background miss table\n73|drives five report shapes. Four plants that admit exactly one realistic member each SURVIVED the\n74|full committed suite in both passes; each is KILLED by a reviewer probe that passes on the\n75|untouched candidate:\n76|\n77|| Row | Plant (readiness.go / acquire.go) | Member admitted under the plant | Committed suite | Probe |\n78|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n79|| R09 | before `return CheckServerAttested(report.Server, wantGeneration)`: `if RawGeneration == \"\" && !Has(realm) { return nil }` | the zero `RealmAdmission{}` server report with a live same-user generation-bound principal — the realistic nothing-reconciled state (the exact shape rev3 P2-C closed on the foreground path) | **SURVIVED ×2**, `Acquire` returns `Via: broker` for an unattested server | K02 kills |\n80|| R10 | same site: `if RawGeneration == \"\" && Has(realm) { return nil }` | rows present, generation empty, wanted generation bound | **SURVIVED ×2** | K03 kills |\n81|| R19 | same site: `if Has(\"headless_creation\") && !Has(realm) { return nil }` | decoy-only admission with a bound generation — the member the foreground entry pins via `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested` | **SURVIVED ×2** | K05 kills |\n82|| R18 | inside the miss arm, after `checkCreationAllowed` refuses: `if req.Deps.ProbeServer != nil && req.Deps.Spawn != nil { return acquireForeground(req, socket) }` | a background miss whose `Dependencies` carry the foreground probe — realistic, because the lifecycle adapter passes one shared `Dependencies` value to every caller | **SURVIVED ×2**: no committed background test arms `ProbeServer`, so the spy census (`Spawn`) never observes the fallback; the unguarded shape (`D-background-fallback`) is still killed by 11 tests | K04 kills |\n83|\n84|Why this is one class: the broker path drives exactly two server-admission shapes (`{gen, no\n85|rows}` as \"unattested server\" and `{rows, stale gen}` as \"stale server admission\") and one\n86|dependency shape (`Spawn` armed, `ProbeServer` nil). Rejection pattern (b) as stated in every\n87|brief of this task — \"if a rule is implemented TWICE (… an exported entry and its internal\n88|sibling), each side needs its own narrowing mutant\" — applies: the \"attested server\" rule is\n89|pinned at the helper (`TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct`) and at the foreground\n90|entry, but the broker-side wiring in `CheckBrokerContact` has no row that admits a member, and\n91|rows 27/28/31 are measured for one fixture each. The DoD lines \"negative tests that fail when the\n92|gate admits what it must reject\" and \"every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant\" are not met\n93|for the broker-side attested-server wiring; the no-fallback proof has a blind spot keyed on the\n94|sibling dependency. Production is correct today; the fix is tests plus rows:\n95|\n96|1. extend `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable` with three subtests — zero\n97|   `RealmAdmission{}`, `{Admitted: realm row, RawGeneration: \"\"}`, `{Admitted: decoy only,\n98|   RawGeneration: bound}` — asserting the literal `capability_unavailable`, exit 6, the five typed\n99|   details, zero spawns (K02/K03/K05 are the templates), and mirror the three rows in\n100|   `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact`;\n101|2. ship a narrowing row at the `CheckBrokerContact` server wiring (the R09 shape; R10/R19 may\n102|   share the anchor) and name it under rows 27/28/36;\n103|3. arm a fail-if-called `ProbeServer` spy in every background miss test (at least the two miss\n104|   tables and `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating`), so that a fallback through the\n105|   foreground path is visible; ship it as a second labelled additive row\n106|   (`D-background-fallback-foreground`, the R18 shape) and extend the row-31 / README sentence to\n107|   say the census arms both foreground dependencies.\n108|\n109|## P3 — fix in the same rework\n110|\n111|- **P3-A. The absence classifier's reject class is pinned at the entry for the mode and\n112|  containment members only.** Reviewer row R01 (`runtimeAbsent` widened to admit\n113|  `runtime ownership`) **SURVIVED ×2**: no committed background `Acquire` test stages foreign\n114|  ownership (the ownership gate is pinned at the helper by `TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesForeignOwnership`\n115|  on both entries, and R13 shows the verify-side wiring is killed there), so a foreign-owned leaf\n116|  on the background path would return `capability_unavailable` with the custody `*Error` as its\n117|  redacted cause — refusal-to-refusal, but the misclassification row 52 forbids (\"an unsafe leaf\n118|  keeps its custody code (top-level *Error, never the unavailable wrapper)\"). Probe K01 (background\n119|  `Acquire` + the `effectiveUID` seam → top-level `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime ownership`,\n120|  broker not probed, spawn 0) passes on the candidate and kills R01. Add it as\n121|  `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` under row 52, or state the ownership member as\n122|  helper-pinned only.\n123|- **P3-B. A censusable \"before\" that is false.** acquire.go:140-143 (\"Refusals precede side\n124|  effects: malformed input, ambient reuse, and missing dependencies all refuse before any directory\n125|  is created\") and results.md:61-62 (\"refuses malformed input, ambient reuse, and missing\n126|  dependencies before any side effect\"). Probe P01: a foreground request with `SessionID =\n127|  \"12345\"` **creates `<root>/tmux` and calls `ProbeServer` before** refusing `tmux_invalid_arguments\n128|  at session identity` (spawn 0). The session identity is malformed input; `acquireForeground`\n129|  validates it only inside `BuildArgv`, after `EnsureRuntimeDir` and the probe. Either parse the\n130|  session (`scalar.ParseUUIDv7`) at the `Acquire` entry before any side effect and add the\n131|  no-directory/no-probe assertions to `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession` (row 45), or\n132|  reword both sentences to the members that are true (caller, realm details, root/name grammar,\n133|  override, collision, dependencies). Rejection pattern (f).\n134|\n135|## Observations (not findings; a sentence each in TRACEABILITY if the producer agrees)\n136|\n137|1. Probe P02: a comma inside the runtime root (`<root>/a,b`, admitted by the POSIX grammar) makes\n138|   `tmuxEnvSocket` split at the wrong comma, so a `TMUX` value naming the derived socket in the\n139|   real encoding walks past the collision gate and `Acquire` spawns. tmux(1) itself splits `TMUX`\n140|   at the first comma, so the decoding is faithful to the source of the encoding; worth a clause in\n141|   row 23/B16 (\"roots containing a comma are outside the TMUX member's encoding\").\n142|2. Probe P03: a cwd-relative spelling of the derived socket (`tmux/ax.sock` with the process cwd\n143|   at the root) walks past the cleaned-string collision gate — the same bound class as the B16\n144|   symlink alias (no path equivalence is applied); B16 could say \"symlinked or relative alias\".\n145|3. Probe P04: `Dependencies.Spawn` is inert on the background path (nil spawner + live broker\n146|   contacts) — consistent with the design; it is what makes P2-A's R18 realistic, since the shared\n147|   struct carries both foreground dependencies on a background call.\n148|4. Probe P05: a `linux` request on this darwin host commits and verifies the same unix custody on\n149|   both callers (row 14 through `Acquire`, not only `EnsureRuntimeDir`).\n150|5. Probe P06: an invalid-UTF-8 typed detail (`Generation = \"gen\\xff\"`) passes the entry's\n151|   non-empty check, is probed against the broker, and then reaches the constructor-failure arm\n152|   `backgroundUnavailable` → `tmux_invalid_arguments at realm details` (acquire.go:289-291) — an\n153|   input-reachable refusal arm with no committed test, not listed under B15 (whose members are all\n154|   seam-only). A 10,000-character remediation is admitted by the landed detail bound. Pin it with\n155|   one subtest or list it under B15 as input-reachable; note that the broker probe precedes the\n156|   refusal. While editing B15: the coverprofile also shows the commit-side leaf-`Stat` arm\n157|   (runtime_unix.go:76-79) and the `secprim.NewGuard` refusal arm (runtime.go:94-96) uncovered;\n158|   both are the same unstageable/unreachable class as their listed siblings but are not named in\n159|   the list.\n160|6. The producer archive's `static-gates.log` is empty and no exit codes for the\n161|   `GOOS=windows`/`GOOS=linux` vet and test-compile gates are recorded anywhere in the archive; the\n162|   green claims live in the results prose only. Rerun here (all exit 0), so not a finding — but\n163|   record the exits next time.\n164|7. Coverage: the uncovered `background fallback` arm (acquire.go:203) is reachable only under a\n165|   weakened `checkCreationAllowed`; `N-creation-literal` exercises it under mutation, which is the\n166|   intended design (rev2 F1). Fine as is.\n167|\n168|## §M — reviewer battery (20 rows, two passes, `battery/reviewer_battery.py` in the evidence archive)\n169|\n170|Every row: anchor count verified (all 20 applied, none NOT_APPLIED, none COMPILE_FAIL), pl