d at the entry only for the fixture shapes: three realistic server-admission shapes and one realistic fallback guard walk through the committed suite\n67|\n68|SPEC §4.2 1419-1424: a background caller \"MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua\n69|broker and its **attested** AX tmux server; if neither exists it MUST return\n70|`capability_unavailable` … and MUST NOT fall back to direct server creation.\" The candidate\n71|implements both halves correctly (`CheckBrokerContact` → `CheckServerAttested`; no spawn call on\n72|the path; `checkCreationAllowed` consulted by call), and the committed background miss table\n73|drives five report shapes. Four plants that admit exactly one realistic member each SURVIVED the\n74|full committed suite in both passes; each is KILLED by a reviewer probe that passes on the\n75|untouched candidate:\n76|\n77|| Row | Plant (readiness.go / acquire.go) | Member admitted under the plant | Committed suite | Probe |\n78|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n79|| R09 | before `return CheckServerAttested(report.Server, wantGeneration)`: `if RawGeneration == \"\" && !Has(realm) { return nil }` | the zero `RealmAdmission{}` server report with a live same-user generation-bound principal — the realistic nothing-reconciled state (the exact shape rev3 P2-C closed on the foreground path) | **SURVIVED ×2**, `Acquire` returns `Via: broker` for an unattested server | K02 kills |\n80|| R10 | same site: `if RawGeneration == \"\" && Has(realm) { return nil }` | rows present, generation empty, wanted generation bound | **SURVIVED ×2** | K03 kills |\n81|| R19 | same site: `if Has(\"headless_creation\") && !Has(realm) { return nil }` | decoy-only admission with a bound generation — the member the foreground entry pins via `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested` | **SURVIVED ×2** | K05 kills |\n82|| R18 | inside the miss arm, after `checkCreationAllowed` refuses: `if req.Deps.ProbeServer != nil && req.Deps.Spawn != nil { return acquireForeground(req, socket) }` | a background miss whose `Dependencies` carry the foreground probe — realistic, because the lifecycle adapter passes one shared `Dependencies` value to every caller | **SURVIVED ×2**: no committed background test arms `ProbeServer`, so the spy census (`Spawn`) never observes the fallback; the unguarded shape (`D-background-fallback`) is still killed by 11 tests | K04 kills |\n83|\n84|Why this is one class: the broker path drives exactly two server-admission shapes (`{gen, no\n85|rows}` as \"unattested server\" and `{rows, stale gen}` as \"stale server admission\") and one\n86|dependency shape (`Spawn` armed, `ProbeServer` nil). Rejection pattern (b) as stated in every\n87|brief of this task — \"if a rule is implemented TWICE (… an exported entry and its internal\n88|sibling), each side needs its own narrowing mutant\" — applies: the \"attested server\" rule is\n89|pinned at the helper (`TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct`) and at the foreground\n90|entry, but the broker-side wiring in `CheckBrokerContact` has no row that admits a member, and\n91|rows 27/28/31 are measured for one fixture each. The DoD lines \"negative tests that fail when the\n92|gate admits what it must reject\" and \"every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant\" are not met\n93|for the broker-side attested-server wiring; the no-fallback proof has a blind spot keyed on the\n94|sibling dependency. Production is correct today; the fix is tests plus rows:\n95|\n96|1. extend `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable` with three subtests — zero\n97|   `RealmAdmission{}`, `{Admitted: realm row, RawGeneration: \"\"}`, `{Admitted: decoy only,\n98|   RawGeneration: bound}` — asserting the literal `capability_unavailable`, exit 6, the five typed\n99|   details, zero spawns (K02/K03/K05 are the templates), and mirror the three rows in\n100|   `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact`;\n101|2. ship a narrowing row at the `CheckBrokerContact` server wiring (the R09 shape; R10/R19 may\n102|   share the anchor) and name it under rows 27/28/36;\n103|3. arm a fail-if-called `ProbeServer` spy in every background miss test (at least the two miss\n104|   tables and `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating`), so that a fallback through the\n105|   foreground path is visible; ship it as a second labelled additive row\n106|   (`D-background-fallback-foreground`, the R18 shape) and extend the row-31 / README sentence to\n107|   say the census arms both foreground dependencies.\n108|\n109|## P3 — fix in the same rework\n110|\n111|- **P3-A. The absence classifier's reject class is pinned at the entry for the mode and\n112|  containment members only.** Reviewer row R01 (`runtimeAbsent` widened to admit\n113|  `runtime ownership`) **SURVIVED ×2**: no committed background `Acquire` test stages foreign\n114|  ownership (the ownership gate is pinned at the helper by `TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesForeignOwnership`\n115|  on both entries, and R13 shows the verify-side wiring is killed there), so a foreign-owned leaf\n116|  on the background path would return `capability_unavailable` with the custody `*Error` as its\n117|  redacted cause — refusal-to-refusal, but the misclassification row 52 forbids (\"an unsafe leaf\n118|  keeps its custody code (top-level *Error, never the unavailable wrapper)\"). Probe K01 (background\n119|  `Acquire` + the `effectiveUID` seam → top-level `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime ownership`,\n120|  broker not probed, spawn 0) passes on the candidate and kills R01. Add it as\n121|  `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` under row 52, or state the ownership member as\n122|  helper-pinned only.\n123|- **P3-B. A censusable \"before\" that is false.** acquire.go:140-143 (\"Refusals precede side\n124|  effects: malformed input, ambient reuse, and missing dependencies all refuse before any directory\n125|  is created\") and results.md:61-62 (\"refuses malformed input, ambient reuse, and missing\n126|  dependencies before any side effect\"). Probe P01: a foreground request with `SessionID =\n127|  \"12345\"` **creates `<root>/tmux` and calls `ProbeServer` before** refusing `tmux_invalid_arguments\n128|  at session identity` (spawn 0). The session identity is malformed input; `acquireForeground`\n129|  validates it only inside `BuildArgv`, after `EnsureRuntimeDir` and the probe. Either parse the\n130|  session (`scalar.ParseUUIDv7`) at the `Acquire` entry before any side effect and add the\n131|  no-directory/no-probe assertions to `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession` (row 45), or\n132|  reword both sentences to the members that are true (caller, realm details, root/name grammar,\n133|  override, collision, dependencies). Rejection pattern (f).\n134|\n135|## Observations (not findings; a sentence each in TRACEABILITY if the producer agrees)\n136|\n137|1. Probe P02: a comma inside the runtime root (`<root>/a,b`, admitted by the POSIX grammar) makes\n138|   `tmuxEnvSocket` split at the wrong comma, so a `TMUX` value naming the derived socket in the\n139|   real encoding walks past the collision gate and `Acquire` spawns. tmux(1) itself splits `TMUX`\n140|   at the first comma, so the decoding is faithful to the source of the encoding; worth a clause in\n141|   row 23/B16 (\"roots containing a comma are outside the TMUX member's encoding\").\n142|2. Probe P03: a cwd-relative spelling of the derived socket (`tmux/ax.sock` with the process cwd\n143|   at the root) walks past the cleaned-string collision gate — the same bound class as the B16\n144|   symlink alias (no path equivalence is applied); B16 could say \"symlinked or relative alias\".\n145|3. Probe P04: `Dependencies.Spawn` is inert on the background path (nil spawner + live broker\n146|   contacts) — consistent with the design; it is what makes P2-A's R18 realistic, since the shared\n147|   struct carries both foreground dependencies on a background call.\n148|4. Probe P05: a `linux` request on this darwin host commits and verifies the same unix custody on\n149|   both callers (row 14 through `Acquire`, not only `EnsureRuntimeDir`).\n150|5. Probe P06: an invalid-UTF-8 typed detail (`Generation = \"gen\\xff\"`) passes the entry's\n151|   non-empty check, is probed against the broker, and then reaches the constructor-failure arm\n152|   `backgroundUnavailable` → `tmux_invalid_arguments at realm details` (acquire.go:289-291) — an\n153|   input-reachable refusal arm with no committed test, not listed under B15 (whose members are all\n154|   seam-only). A 10,000-character remediation is admitted by the landed detail bound. Pin it with\n155|   one subtest or list it under B15 as input-reachable; note that the broker probe precedes the\n156|   refusal. While editing B15: the coverprofile also shows the commit-side leaf-`Stat` arm\n157|   (runtime_unix.go:76-79) and the `secprim.NewGuard` refusal arm (runtime.go:94-96) uncovered;\n158|   both are the same unstageable/unreachable class as their listed siblings but are not named in\n159|   the list.\n160|6. The producer archive's `static-gates.log` is empty and no exit codes for the\n161|   `GOOS=windows`/`GOOS=linux` vet and test-compile gates are recorded anywhere in the archive; the\n162|   green claims live in the results prose only. Rerun here (all exit 0), so not a finding — but\n163|   record the exits next time.\n164|7. Coverage: the uncovered `background fallback` arm (acquire.go:203) is reachable only under a\n165|   weakened `checkCreationAllowed`; `N-creation-literal` exercises it under mutation, which is the\n166|   intended design (rev2 F1). Fine as is.\n167|\n168|## §M — reviewer battery (20 rows, two passes, `battery/reviewer_battery.py` in the evidence archive)\n169|\n170|Every row: anchor count verified (all 20 applied, none NOT_APPLIED, none COMPILE_FAIL), plant\n171|applied to the mutant copy, the committed suite run as shipped (full package, `-count=1 -v`, no\n172|`-run` mask), exit + raw output logged, file restored from a byte copy and re-compared, package\n173|directory hash equal before/after (`c8eb3ed00bc20f82`), `internal/` re-diffed against the\n174|candidate copy after each pass. Rows predicted SURVIVED were additionally run with\n175|`zz_review_probe_test.go` present and the named killer selected (`*.with-probe.log`).\n176|\n177|| Row | Kind | Gate (site) | Committed suite | With probe | Killer(s) |\n178|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n179|| R01-absence-admits-ownership | narrowing | `runtimeAbsent` admits `runtime ownership` (acquire.go:252) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K01 (P3-A) |\n180|| R02-absence-admits-containment | narrowing | `runtimeAbsent` admits `runtime containment` (acquire.go:252) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf |\n181|| R03-absence-admits-mode-rev4R05 | replay | `runtimeAbsent` admits `runtime mode` (acquire.go:252) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal |\n182|| R04-name-literal-lexical-site | narrowing | `\"ax-tmux\"` at the Acquire lexical step (acquire.go:151) | KILLED | — | 18 tests incl. TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath/{foreground,background} |\n183|| R05-name-literal-ensure-site | narrowing | `\"ax-tmux\"` at the foreground ensure (acquire.go:217) | KILLED | — | 8 tests incl. TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath/foreground, TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer |\n184|| R06-name-literal-verify-site | narrowing | `\"ax-tmux\"` at the background verify (acquire.go:179) | KILLED | — | 6 tests incl. TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath/background, TestAcquireBackgroundContactsBroker |\n185|| R07-absence-only-macos-rev4R14 | replay | absence remap limited to macOS (acquire.go:180) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating/{linux,wsl2} |\n186|| R08-spy-guarded-plant-top | additive | guarded `Spawn` call at the top of `acquireBackground` (acquire.go:176) | KILLED (11 top-level tests, 20 lines) | — | every background-path Acquire test that enters the function |\n187|| R09-broker-empty-admission-admits | narrowing | broker-side server wiring admits the zero admission (readiness.go:86) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K02 (P2-A) |\n188|| R10-broker-empty-generation-admits | narrowing | same site, admits rows-without-generation | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K03 (P2-A) |\n189|| R11-details-drop-generation | narrowing | typed-details gate drops the generation member (acquire.go:148) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireRefusesMissingRealmDetails/generation (reroute to `dependencies`) |\n190|| R12-details-drop-brokerstate | narrowing | same, broker-state member | KILLED | — | TestAcquireRefusesMissingRealmDetails/broker_state (reroute) |\n191|| R13-verify-ownership-wiring-drop | narrowing | verify side consults `verifyOwnership` and drops the verdict (runtime_unix.go:134) | KILLED | — | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesForeignOwnership (Verify leg) |\n192|| R14-argv-drop-detached | narrowing | `-d` removed from the spawn vector (argv.go:28) | KILLED | — | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket |\n193|| R15-argv-tail-attach | narrowing | `ax pane` → `ax attach` (argv.go:30) | KILLED | — | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket, TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer |\n194|| R16-verify-mode-group-bits-only | replay | verify mode `!= 0700` → `&0o077 != 0` (runtime_unix.go:131) | KILLED | — | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNarrowerMode/{0600,0500} |\n195|| R17-commit-nofollow-drop | replay | drop `O_NOFOLLOW` on the commit Openat (runtime_unix.go:59) | KILLED | — | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf |\n196|| R18-fallback-via-foreground-guarded | additive | fallback into `acquireForeground` guarded on `ProbeServer` (acquire.go:200-202) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K04 (P2-A) |\n197|| R19-broker-decoy-admission-admits | narrowing | broker-side server wiring admits a decoy-only admission (readiness.go:86) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K05 (P2-A) |\n198|| C-reviewer-control | control | comment-only edit in readiness.go | SURVIVED | — | (must survive; proves the battery observes outcomes) |\n199|\n200|Denominator: 20 applied rows = 13 narrowing + 4 replay + 2 additive + 1 control. Of the 13\n201|narrowings, 9 KILLED by the committed suite, 4 SURVIVED (R01, R09, R10, R19), each proven real by\n202|a probe kill (production correct, suite blind). Of the 2 additives, R08 KILLED and R18 SURVIVED\n203|(probe kill). All 4 replays KILLED — the rev4 closures hold. Every KILLED row was killed by exactly\n204|the tests named above (kill lines in the raw logs).\n205|\n206|## §P — reviewer probes (11, `logs/probes-rev5.log`)\n207|\n208|K01 background + foreign ownership → top-level `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime ownership`,\n209|broker not probed, spawn 0 (baseline for R01); K02 broker path + zero `RealmAdmission{}` →\n210|`capability_unavailable`, spawn 0, and `CheckBrokerContact` → `server attestation` (baseline for\n211|R09); K03 broker path + admitted-without-generation → `capability_unavailable` / `server\n212|generation` (R10); K04 background miss with `ProbeServer` AND `Spawn` armed → typed unavailable,\n213|neither dependency called (R18); K05 broker path + decoy-only admission → `capability_unavailable`\n214|(R19); P01 malformed session creates the directory and probes the server before refusing (P3-B);\n215|P02 comma-root TMUX encoding walks through (obs 1); P03 relative alias walks through (obs 2); P04\n216|nil spawner on the background path contacts (obs 3); P05 linux request on both callers (obs 4);\n217|P06 invalid-UTF-8 generation reaches the constructor-failure arm after the broker probe, a 10k\n218|remediation is admitted (obs 5).\n219|\n220|## What held under attack (keep)\n221|\n222|- Dedicated-server rule per vector: override refused on all five members plus whitespace through\n223|  `Acquire` with no spawn and no directory; byte-identical, cleaned and real-encoding collisions\n224|  refused; argv gate refuses all five and the vector is pinned element-by-element (R14/R15 KILLED);\n225|  `Acquire` never reads the environment or execs; the §3.2 path is now pinned at the entry on both\n226|  callers and at all three `RuntimeDirName` sites (R04/R05/R06 KILLED).\n227|- Background rules: broker-or-refuse with the literal `capability_unavailable`, exit 6 and the\n228|  five typed details asserted as literals; the absent-leaf cold state returns the typed refusal on\n229|  macOS, Linux and WSL2 with no probe, no spawn and no directory (R07 KILLED); the unguarded\n230|  fallback is killed by 11 tests (R08, D-background-fallback); same-user generation-bound broker\n231|  principal at the entry (producer N-broker-uid/-generation reproduced). The residue is P2-A.\n232|- Attestation: landed `terminalbackend.Admitted` consumed through `Has` composed with the\n233|  generation equality; the foreground running arm is pinned at the entry for empty admissions;\n234|  stale, decoy and both-empty shapes refuse at the helper and on the foreground entry.\n235|- Custody: the top-level oracle now sees the wrapper (R03 KILLED; old-oracle replay SURVIVES the\n236|  same mutant); mode/containment members of the absence class pinned at the background entry;\n237|  FIFO and regular-file leaves refuse on both entries without blocking; symlink leaf refuses on\n238|  both entries (R17 KILLED); exact 0700 on both sides (R16 KILLED); ownership wiring on both sides\n239|  (R13 KILLED); read-only root, missing root, handle mismatch refuse; the real-SIGKILL crash test\n240|  converges.\n241|- Determinism: 0 SKIP with tmux unresolvable, 140 RUN; no real-tmux witness (B1).\n242|- Boundary: `internal/traceability` untouched; README section carries no CLI/capability claim; no\n243|  trunk drift; producer evidence archive complete and digest-verified; LOGBOOK newest-first.\n244|\n245|## Coverage ratio measured against the 58-row table\n246|\n247|**58 of 58 rows are driven as their statements are written**; the ratio is not inflated. The\n248|gaps sit beside the statements, at the member level: rows 27/28/36 (the broker-path \"attested\n249|server\" conjunct is driven for two of five admission shapes — P2-A), row 31 (the no-fallback\n250|census arms `Spawn` only — P2-A), row 52 (the custody-code half is measured for the mode and\n251|containment members, not ownership — P3-A), and acquire.go:140-143 claims a \"before\" that row 45\n252|does not measure (P3-B).\n253|\n254|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n255|\n256|1. **P2-A (tests + rows, no production change required)**: add the zero-admission,\n257|   admitted-without-generation and decoy-only server shapes to\n258|   `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable` and `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact`\n259|   (K02/K03/K05 in the reviewer probe file are the templates); ship a narrowing row at the\n260|   `CheckBrokerContact` server wiring (R09 shape) named under rows 27/28/36; arm a fail-if-called\n261|   `ProbeServer` spy in the background miss tests and `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating`,\n262|   ship the R18 shape as a labelled additive row, and extend the row-31/README sentence to say the\n263|   census arms both foreground dependencies.\n264|2. **P3-A**: `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` (K01 template) named under row 52, or\n265|   state the ownership member as helper-pinned only.\n266|3. **P3-B**: validate the session identity at the `Acquire` entry before `EnsureRuntimeDir` and\n267|   the probe (and assert no directory / no probe in `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession`),\n268|   or reword acquire.go:140-143 and the results sentence to the members that are true.\n269|4. Optional sentences: comma-root and relative-alias scoping under row 23/B16; the\n270|   input-reachable constructor-failure arm under B15 or a subtest; record static-gate exit codes in\n271|   the archive.\n272|5. Rerun the package suite (tmux hidden), `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...`, the harness\n273|   twice, and the 30-command suite; refresh results/matrix/archive; hand off as revision 6.\n274|   Everything in \"What held under attack\" needs no change — do not re-litigate it.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
