{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c683","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c52f-2ee9-7e90-86a5-5469e2a72bf6"},"sequence":412,"recorded_at":1780531400000819,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0c8ad2d8-68e1-4b10-83fc-51c6169a80fc","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0c8ad2d8-68e1-4b10-83fc-51c6169a80fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0c8ad2d8-68e1-4b10-83fc-51c6169a80fc"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c53d-fd31-71d3-b0d9-8df193cf00a9"},"task_id":"01a0c53d-fd31-71d3-b0d9-8df193cf00a9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c53d-fd31-71d3-b0d9-8df193cf00a9","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev6-read/matrix.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-35urbp conformance matrix — implement-private-tmux-server-management (rev5)\n2|\n3|Authority: pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`. Every row names the\n4|spec clause in the spec's own words, the production call site, and the\n5|named committed test that drives it through that entry. 58 of 58 rows\n6|driven (row 55 extends the rows 19-22 override class with the fifth\n7|ambient member; row 56 binds the Section 3.2 path and runtime-root\n8|clause; rows 57-58 pin the commit-failure and whitespace-override\n9|arms). Bounds B1-B21 are stated in\n10|`internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`. Changes from rev4: rows 16/56\n11|name the new entry-level spec-path test on both callers (the runtime\n12|leaf is no longer an `Acquire` input), row 52 names the\n13|macos/linux/wsl2 absence subtests and the top-level custody oracle,\n14|row 6 states the ELOOP darwin-equivalence, row 23 scopes the live\n15|collision members, B15/B16/B19 gain the observation sentences, and the\n16|mutant map carries one new narrowing row (`N-absence-remap-widen`)\n17|plus the rewritten `N-background-absence-remap`.\n18|\n19|Attestation authority: sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature\n20|verification, liveness, and expiry are the landed\n21|`internal/terminalbackend` Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission verdict,\n22|consumed here as an `Admitted` set composed only with the generation\n23|equality `internal/axpane` checkRealm enforces. This leaf decides\n24|membership plus generation binding and re-decides nothing.\n25|\n26|## §3.2 socket path and runtime root\n27|\n28|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n29||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n30|| 56 | Dedicated socket is `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC root (macOS: per-user temporary directory; Linux/WSL2: `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax`), resolved by the landed localstore layout as PathRuntime and supplied by the caller; the socket is runtime IPC, never durable identity. The runtime leaf is not an Acquire input: the entry always passes RuntimeDirName, so the outcome socket is `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths | `SocketPath` (socket.go), `Acquire` (acquire.go) | TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir, TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath (foreground, background) |\n31|\n32|## §4.2 dedicated -S server; no ambient/default discovery or reuse\n33|\n34|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n35||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n36|| 16 | AX MUST use its dedicated `-S` server, as `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` with both leaves asserted as spec literals; the Acquire outcome socket equals `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths | `SocketPath` (socket.go), `Acquire` (acquire.go) | TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir, TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath (foreground, background) |\n37|| 17 | MUST NOT discover or reuse the default server by ambient socket name, under hostile ambient on all five members | `ResolveSocket` (socket.go) | TestResolveSocketDerivesIgnoringAmbient |\n38|| 18 | Ambient facts observed without use | `ObserveAmbient` (socket.go) | TestObserveAmbientRecordsWithoutUsing, TestObserveAmbientNilLookupKeepsOutOfBand |\n39|| 19 | Environment-variable vector refuses with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/environment_variable |\n40|| 20 | Inherited-socket vector refuses with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/inherited_socket |\n41|| 21 | Default-path vector refuses with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/default_path |\n42|| 22 | Conventional-name vector refuses with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/conventional_name |\n43|| 55 | TMUX_TMPDIR vector refuses with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/tmux_tmpdir |\n44|| 58 | Whitespace-only override refuses with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/whitespace_only, TestResolveSocketRefusesEveryOverrideVector/whitespace_only |\n45|| 23 | Ambient value colliding with the derived socket refuses on every member, byte-identical and unclean (`/./`, `//`) spellings alike, and the TMUX member in the real `<socket>,<pid>,<index>` encoding. Only TMUXEnv and InheritedSocket can name the derived socket in real tmux semantics; the other three members pin defence-in-depth shapes | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollision (5 subtests), TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollision (5 subtests), TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollisionUncleanSpellings (2 subtests), TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollisionUncleanSpelling, TestResolveSocketRefusesTMUXEnvRealEncoding, TestAcquireRefusesTMUXEnvCollisionRealEncoding |\n46|| 40 | Absent server spawns dedicated with exact -S argv disjoint from every ambient vector | `Acquire` via `BuildArgv` | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer |\n47|| 41 | Running attested dedicated server attaches with no second spawn | `Acquire` | TestAcquireForegroundAttachesToRunningAttested |\n48|| 46 | Spawn vector carries the dedicated -S socket | `BuildArgv` (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket |\n49|| 47 | Ambient sockets refuse at the spawn vector on all five members | `BuildArgv` (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvRefusesAmbientSocket (5 subtests) |\n50|\n51|## §4.2 credential-sensitive creation; background broker-or-refuse\n52|\n53|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n54||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n55|| 24 | A background CLI MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and its attested AX tmux server (macOS) | `Acquire` via `CheckBrokerContact` | TestAcquireBackgroundContactsBroker |\n56|| 25 | If neither exists it MUST return `capability_unavailable` with typed realm/readiness details: no broker | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/no_broker |\n57|| 26 | Same: foreign-user broker | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/foreign-user_broker |\n58|| 27 | Same: unattested server | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/unattested_server |\n59|| 28 | Same: stale-generation admission | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/stale_server_admission, .../generation-unbound_principal |\n60|| 29 | Linux background miss likewise refuses without fallback | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissOnLinuxAlsoRefusesWithoutFallback |\n61|| 30 | Broker probe failure is unknown, never unavailable, with no spawn | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundProbeFailurePassesThrough |\n62|| 31 | A Background caller MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server; MUST NOT fall back to direct server creation | `checkCreationAllowed` via `Acquire` | TestCheckCreationAllowedRefusesBackground, TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable (N-creation-literal kill path) |\n63|| 42 | Running unattested server refuses with no spawn and no repair, including zero admission rows and an empty generation | `Acquire` | Te